.tactic = flow:narrative

.what = procedural code reads as flat, linear code paragraphs — guard clauses, then the main path. no else, no nested if
.how:
  - early returns and throws in place of if/else (`if (!input.email) return failure();`)
  - code paragraphs: 1–5 lines per task, each under a one-line `//` title, a blank line between
  - a deep nest → split into its own procedure
```ts
// validate input format
const isValid = validateShape(input);
if (!isValid) return failure();

// attempt fallback
const found = tryToFind(input);
if (!found) MalfunctionError.throw('fallback failed');
```
.enforcement: else and nested if = blocker; a multi-line block with no paragraph title = blocker
